-- Why: the growth department's positions (brand_mgr, marketing_content, marketing_analyst,
-- marketing_social, marketing_design, optimisation_eng, sales_director) are certified against six
-- external bodies. This file authors ONLY the question banks for those six certifications, at the
-- real exams' difficulty: scenario and application items, four options, one key, a two-sentence
-- rationale, the syllabus area named as the issuing body names it, ~25% marked 'hard', keys spread
-- evenly across A/B/C/D, never "all of the above". The role_certification rows and the sitter are
-- authored by a sibling engineer and are deliberately NOT touched here.
--
-- Each bank is guarded by `where not exists (... certification = '<name>')` so a bank is authored
-- once even if two authors share a certification; the first author's bank stands.
--
-- Apply: node scripts/apply_sql.mjs scripts/sql/certifications_growth.sql --apply --ddl

-- ============================================================================
-- CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing (CIM) — 40 questions
-- ============================================================================
insert into public.certification_exam_question
  (certification, syllabus_area, difficulty, question, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_option, rationale)
select * from (values
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing and Digital Strategy','exam','A B2B marketplace has AED 15,000 a month for demand generation and must choose between broad display awareness and search against high-intent procurement keywords. On what basis should the decision be made?','Expected cost per qualified request for quotation from each channel at current conversion rates','The channel with the larger addressable reach','The channel the nearest competitor invests in most heavily','The channel with the lowest cost per thousand impressions','A','At a constrained budget the strategic test is cost per qualified commercial outcome, not exposure. Reach and CPM say nothing about how many buyers actually submit a request.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing and Digital Strategy','exam','A marketing director maps the organisation against Ansoff. The firm already serves UAE construction buyers and now wants to sell the same marketplace to UAE hospitality buyers. Which quadrant is this?','Market penetration','Market development','Product development','Diversification','B','A new customer segment served with the existing proposition is market development. Product development would require changing the offer, and diversification would change both.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing and Digital Strategy','exam','A PESTEL scan for a Gulf marketplace flags the introduction of a 9% corporate tax above AED 375,000 of profit. Where does this belong and what is the marketing consequence?','Social, requiring a change of brand tone','Technological, requiring new platform features','Economic and Legal, requiring pricing and margin assumptions to be revisited','Environmental, requiring sustainability reporting','C','Fiscal policy sits in the economic and legal strands of PESTEL. Its marketing consequence is on price architecture and contribution assumptions, not on tone or features.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing and Digital Strategy','hard','Two segments show equal revenue. Segment A costs AED 900 to acquire and churns at 40% a year; segment B costs AED 1,400 and churns at 12%. Budget is fixed. Which allocation argument is strongest?','Fund A, because its acquisition cost is lower','Fund B, because a lower churn rate always signals a better segment','Split evenly, because both segments contribute equal revenue','Fund B, because its longer expected tenure produces a higher lifetime value per dirham of acquisition cost','D','Allocation is decided by lifetime value relative to acquisition cost, not by either figure alone. B recovers its higher cost over a materially longer expected tenure.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Innovation in Marketing','exam','A marketplace pilots a new instant-quote feature with 30 suppliers before a full release. Which innovation practice does this represent?','A stage-gate pilot that reduces launch risk by testing with a limited cohort','A line extension','A brand repositioning','A harvest strategy','A','Testing with a limited cohort before wider release is the classic pilot gate. It buys information about real behaviour at a fraction of full launch cost.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Innovation in Marketing','exam','Adoption of a new supplier verification badge is slow among established suppliers but fast among new joiners. Which diffusion insight best explains this?','New joiners have higher disposable budgets','Perceived relative advantage is higher where no incumbent process is being displaced','The badge lacks trialability for everyone equally','Observability is irrelevant in B2B markets','B','Rogers holds that adoption tracks perceived relative advantage over the current practice. Established suppliers already have a working process, so the badge offers them less marginal gain.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Innovation in Marketing','exam','A team proposes ten new features. The marketing lead insists each is expressed as a customer problem with a measurable success metric before development. What is the primary benefit?','It shortens the development sprint','It removes the need for user research','It makes post-launch evaluation possible against a stated benchmark','It guarantees the feature will be adopted','C','A stated metric defined before build is what makes evaluation honest afterwards. Without it, any outcome can be rationalised as success.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Innovation in Marketing','hard','An innovation shows strong qualitative enthusiasm in eight depth interviews but flat behaviour in a live test with 4,000 sessions. What should the marketer conclude?','The live test was badly instrumented and should be discarded','The two findings cannot be compared','Eight interviews are sufficient evidence to proceed','Stated preference from a small qualitative sample does not override observed behaviour at scale','D','Qualitative work explains motivation but cannot estimate incidence. Where observed behaviour at scale contradicts stated enthusiasm, behaviour governs the decision.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing Communications','exam','A campaign runs identical creative in Arabic and English. Arabic click-through is strong but Arabic form completion is half the English rate. What is the most likely cause to investigate first?','The landing page and form were not localised, so the journey breaks after the click','Arabic audiences are less interested in the product','The Arabic ad spend was too low','Arabic keywords are inherently more expensive','A','A healthy click with a weak completion isolates the failure to the post-click experience. Translating the advertisement without translating the destination is the common cause.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing Communications','exam','Which objective is written to a standard a CIM examiner would accept for a communications plan?','Increase brand awareness substantially this year','Raise aided awareness among UAE procurement managers from 12% to 20% by 31 December, measured by the same tracking survey','Become the leading marketplace in the region','Improve the quality of our marketing','B','A usable objective states the audience, the measure, the baseline, the target and the deadline. The other options cannot be evaluated as met or missed.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing Communications','exam','A B2B marketplace has a small budget and a long, committee-based buying cycle. Which communications mix emphasis is most defensible?','Heavy television and outdoor to build fame quickly','A single large trade-show stand consuming most of the budget','Content and search that answer procurement questions, plus targeted email nurture to the committee','Broad consumer social advertising','C','Committee buying rewards content that resolves the questions each member asks, sustained over the cycle. Mass fame channels are poorly matched to a narrow buying centre on a small budget.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing Communications','hard','Attribution shows paid search taking credit for most conversions, yet pausing content marketing for a quarter caused branded search volume to fall 30%. What does this indicate?','Content marketing has no measurable value','Branded search volume is not a marketing metric','Paid search should be paused instead','Last-click attribution understates upper-funnel activity that generates the branded demand search later harvests','D','Last-click credits the final touch and blinds the marketer to demand creation upstream. The fall in branded search after pausing content is direct evidence of that upstream contribution.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Digital Customer Experience','exam','A buyer abandons the request-for-quotation form at the field asking for a company trade licence number. Which response follows customer experience practice?','Make the field optional at first submission and collect the licence at supplier matching, when the buyer is committed','Remove all validation from the form','Add an explanatory paragraph above the field and change nothing else','Require the field earlier in the journey','A','Friction should be moved to the point where the buyer already sees value in continuing. Deferring a non-blocking field preserves the lead without abandoning the data need.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Digital Customer Experience','exam','Mapping the buyer journey, the team finds the largest drop between the quotation being issued and the buyer replying. What is the appropriate intervention to design first?','A new acquisition campaign','A prompt and clarification step at the quotation stage, since that is where value is currently lost','A brand refresh','A price reduction across all categories','B','Journey work directs effort to the stage with the largest measured loss. Adding traffic ahead of an unfixed leak simply spends more to lose more.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Digital Customer Experience','exam','Which measure best reflects experience quality at the point of a resolved support interaction?','Annual brand awareness','Total website sessions','Customer satisfaction collected immediately after the resolution, alongside first-contact resolution rate','Share of voice','C','Transactional satisfaction taken at the moment of resolution measures the experience actually delivered. Awareness and traffic measures are unrelated to service quality.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Digital Customer Experience','hard','A firm reports a Net Promoter Score of plus 40 while repeat purchase has fallen for three quarters. Which reading is most professional?','The score is wrong and should be abandoned','The sample must be too small to matter','Repeat purchase is a lagging indicator and can be ignored','Stated advocacy and repeat behaviour are different constructs, so the behavioural decline must be investigated on its own terms','D','Advocacy scores measure sentiment among responders, not purchasing behaviour across the base. A behavioural decline is evidence in its own right and needs its own diagnosis.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Resource Management','exam','A marketing plan requests AED 180,000 for the year. The finance director asks for the return case. Which submission is strongest?','Forecast qualified leads by channel, an assumed close rate with its source, resulting gross profit, and the payback period','A list of planned activities and their costs','A statement that marketing investment is a long-term commitment','Benchmark spend of competitors in the sector','A','A return case connects spend to volume, to conversion and finally to profit, with the assumptions visible. Activity lists and benchmarks do not answer the question asked.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Resource Management','exam','Mid-year, one of four channels is delivering 70% of qualified leads at half the target cost per lead. What is the correct resource response?','Hold the original allocation to preserve the plan','Reallocate incremental budget to the outperforming channel while testing whether performance holds at higher volume','Cut the other three channels immediately','Double every channel budget','B','Plans are revised on evidence, but efficiency at low volume frequently decays as volume rises. Increasing spend in steps while watching cost per lead protects the gain.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Resource Management','exam','A marketing manager must justify hiring an in-house Arabic copywriter versus using an agency. Which analysis is the professional basis?','Preference of the marketing team','The agency rate card alone','Total cost of both options at forecast volume, alongside turnaround time, quality control and the value of retained institutional knowledge','Whether competitors employ in-house writers','C','A make-or-buy decision compares full cost at the expected volume together with the non-cost factors that differ. A rate card alone omits both volume and capability effects.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Resource Management','hard','A campaign delivered 20% more leads than planned but gross profit fell against plan. Which explanation should be tested first?','The market grew and competitors took share','Awareness was too low','The finance system misreported revenue','Lead quality declined, so a higher volume converted at a materially lower rate or at lower order value','D','Volume rising while profit falls points at the mix between the two, which is quality. Testing conversion rate and average order value by source isolates it directly.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing and Digital Strategy','exam','A marketplace positions itself on speed of quotation. Competitors then match the turnaround. What does this reveal about the positioning?','It rested on a capability that was not defensible, so differentiation must be rebuilt on something harder to copy','It was never valued by buyers','Positioning should not be based on service attributes','The firm should reduce price instead','A','Positioning holds only while the underlying advantage resists imitation. A matched attribute stops differentiating and the search moves to a defensible basis.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing and Digital Strategy','exam','Which statement about a value proposition for a two-sided marketplace is correct?','One proposition should serve both sides identically','Buyers and suppliers need distinct propositions, because each side values a different outcome from the same platform','Only the buyer side needs a proposition','Propositions are a consumer marketing concept','B','Each side of a marketplace joins for a different benefit, so each requires its own articulated proposition. A single message inevitably underserves one side.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing Communications','exam','An Arabic-language advertisement is produced by machine translation of English copy and performs poorly. Which corrective action is most appropriate?','Increase the Arabic budget','Abandon Arabic advertising','Commission Arabic copy written for the audience, with the offer and call to action expressed idiomatically, then retest against the English control','Use the English creative for all audiences','C','Language performance is a creative problem before it is a budget problem. Native-written copy tested against the existing control isolates whether the creative was the cause.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Innovation in Marketing','hard','A new pricing tier is launched. Revenue rises but the number of active buyers falls. Which conclusion is best supported before further data?','The launch was a clear success','Buyer count is not a relevant metric','The launch failed and should be reversed at once','The launch may have traded breadth for yield, and the trade-off must be evaluated against the strategy for market coverage','D','Higher revenue on a smaller base is a yield-for-breadth trade, not an unambiguous win. Whether it is acceptable depends on the coverage the strategy requires.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Digital Customer Experience','exam','Which practice best supports a consistent experience across Arabic and English channels?','A shared content and tone framework with language-specific execution and shared measurement definitions','Maintaining separate uncoordinated teams for each language','Publishing English first and translating later in every case','Restricting Arabic to social channels','A','Consistency comes from a common framework and common metric definitions, executed natively in each language. Uncoordinated teams or delayed translation produce divergent experiences.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Resource Management','exam','A quarterly marketing report is prepared for a board. What should lead the report?','A list of campaigns delivered','Performance against the stated objectives, with variance explained and the resulting recommendation','A gallery of creative work','The volume of social media posts','B','A board reads for performance against commitments and the decision implied. Activity inventories do not tell a board whether the plan is working.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing and Digital Strategy','hard','A marketplace has strong buyer demand but too few verified suppliers to fulfil it. Where should the next marketing dirham go?','Buyer acquisition, because demand is proven','Brand advertising to both sides equally','Supplier acquisition and verification, because the constraint on realised transactions sits on the supply side','Price promotion to buyers','C','Marketing spend should relieve the binding constraint on realised value. Adding demand that cannot be fulfilled degrades the buyer experience and wastes acquisition cost.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing Communications','exam','Which media selection is best matched to reaching procurement managers at a firm-level account with a small budget?','Untargeted display across general news sites','Consumer influencer partnerships','Radio sponsorship','Professional network advertising targeted by job function and company size, supported by search on category terms','D','Function and firm targeting reaches the buying centre without paying for irrelevant impressions. Category search then captures the same audience at the moment of intent.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Innovation in Marketing','exam','A team wants to test a new onboarding flow. Which design gives the cleanest read?','Randomised assignment of concurrent traffic to the current and new flows, measured on the same completion definition','Launch it to everyone and compare against last month','Show it only to the most engaged users','Ask the sales team for their impression','A','Concurrent randomised assignment removes seasonality and mix effects that a period-on-period comparison cannot. Selecting engaged users would confound the test with the selection.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Digital Customer Experience','hard','Support tickets fall 40% after a self-service knowledge base launches, while satisfaction also falls. What is the most likely interpretation?','Customers are happier and simply contact support less','Some customers are being deflected without resolution, so contained volume masks unresolved need','The satisfaction survey has become unreliable','Self-service should always reduce satisfaction','B','Deflection reduces contacts whether or not the need was met. A simultaneous satisfaction fall is the signature of containment without resolution.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Resource Management','exam','Which cost belongs in the calculation of cost per acquisition for a paid channel?','Media spend only','All company overheads apportioned equally','Media spend plus the directly attributable agency, creative and platform fees for that channel','Media spend minus any discounts negotiated','C','Cost per acquisition uses the full directly attributable cost of running the channel. Excluding creative and fees flatters the channel and distorts allocation.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing and Digital Strategy','exam','A director asks for the marketing plan to state its critical assumptions explicitly. What is the main professional benefit?','It shortens the plan document','It transfers accountability to the finance function','It removes the need for forecasting','It allows the plan to be corrected quickly when an assumption proves false, rather than the whole plan being defended','D','Explicit assumptions make the plan falsifiable at the level of its parts. When one fails, only that part needs revision.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing Communications','hard','Two creatives are compared over one week: A converts at 3.1% on 480 sessions, B at 2.6% on 510 sessions. What should be reported?','The difference is not distinguishable from noise at this sample size and the test needs more exposure before a decision','A is the winner and should take all budget','B should be discarded immediately','The result proves creative has no effect','A','At a few hundred sessions per arm, a half-point difference falls well within ordinary variation. Reporting a winner here would be reporting noise.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Innovation in Marketing','exam','What distinguishes a minimum viable proposition from an incomplete product?','It is cheaper to build','It is deliberately scoped to test the central commercial assumption while still delivering the core value to a real customer','It has no measurement attached','It is only shown internally','B','A minimum viable proposition is defined by the assumption it tests and the value it still delivers. An incomplete product simply fails the customer.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Digital Customer Experience','exam','Which data practice is required before personalising communications to buyers in the UAE?','No consent is required for business contacts','Consent is only needed for Arabic-language messages','Lawful basis and consent handling under the applicable data protection framework, with a documented purpose and a working opt-out','Consent is needed only for messages containing pricing','C','Personalisation depends on personal data and therefore on a lawful basis and honoured opt-outs. Language and content of the message do not change that obligation.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Resource Management','exam','A campaign is behind plan at week three of twelve. What is the appropriate management action?','Wait until the campaign ends to review','Increase the budget uniformly','Cancel the campaign','Diagnose the stage at which performance diverges, act on that stage, and set a review point to confirm the correction','D','Control is exercised during the period, at the specific stage that diverges. Waiting or spending uniformly both forgo the diagnosis.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing and Digital Strategy','hard','Two segments are equally attractive on size and growth, but only one matches the firm capability and route to market. What does segment selection theory require?','Choose the segment the firm can actually serve profitably with its current capability and access','Choose the larger segment','Choose both to spread risk','Defer the decision until capability is built','A','Segment attractiveness must be weighed against the ability to compete for it. A segment the firm cannot serve profitably is not attractive to that firm.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Marketing Communications','exam','A stakeholder asks why the plan sets different messages for the procurement manager and the finance approver in the same account. What is the correct explanation?','Different messages increase total impressions','Members of a buying centre hold different roles and evaluate the decision on different criteria','It reduces media cost','It is a requirement of the media platform','B','In organisational buying, the user, the influencer and the approver judge against different criteria. A single message cannot address them all with equal force.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Digital Customer Experience','exam','Which is the strongest early warning indicator that experience is deteriorating on a marketplace?','Falling social media follower count','Fewer press mentions','Rising time to first supplier response combined with rising buyer abandonment at the quotation stage','A drop in newsletter open rate','C','Response time and stage abandonment are operational measures of the experience being delivered. The other measures are reputational or channel-specific and lag behind.'),
('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing','Resource Management','hard','A marketing budget must be cut by 30% with two weeks notice. Which approach best preserves commercial performance?','Cut every line by 30%','Cut headcount first','Cut all paid media and retain all agency retainers','Protect the activity with the lowest proven cost per qualified outcome and cut the least proven, stating the expected effect on pipeline','D','A uniform cut damages the best-performing activity as much as the worst. Cutting by proven efficiency preserves the pipeline, and stating the effect keeps the decision honest.')
) as v(certification, syllabus_area, difficulty, question, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_option, rationale)
where not exists (select 1 from public.certification_exam_question where certification = 'CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing');

-- ============================================================================
-- Google Analytics 4 Certification (Google) — 40 questions
-- ============================================================================
insert into public.certification_exam_question
  (certification, syllabus_area, difficulty, question, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_option, rationale)
select * from (values
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Events and parameters','exam','A marketplace wants to know which quotation category a submitted request belongs to. What is the correct GA4 implementation?','Send one generate_lead event with a category event parameter and register it as a custom dimension','Create a separate event name for every category','Store the category in the user_id field','Put the category in the page title only','A','GA4 models behaviour as events carrying parameters, so the varying value belongs in a parameter. Registering it as a custom dimension makes it available in reports and explorations.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Events and parameters','exam','Which statement about automatically collected events in GA4 is correct?','They must be configured in Google Tag Manager before they fire','Events such as first_visit and session_start are collected by the GA4 tag without additional configuration','They can only be seen in the Realtime report','They replace the need for any custom events','B','Automatically collected events fire from the base tag with no extra setup. Custom events are still required for business-specific actions such as a request submission.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Events and parameters','exam','A developer sends an event named Generate_Lead in some places and generate_lead in others. What is the consequence in GA4?','GA4 normalises the casing automatically','Only the first name received is kept','Event names are case sensitive, so two separate events are reported and the metric is split','The property rejects both events','C','GA4 treats event names as case sensitive strings. Inconsistent casing silently fragments what should be a single measured action.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Events and parameters','hard','A custom dimension is registered for lead_source on 14 March. A report for 1 to 31 March shows (not set) for the first half of the month. Why?','The dimension was configured incorrectly','The data retention period expired','GA4 samples the first half of any month','Registration is not retroactive, so events collected before registration have no processed value for that dimension','D','Custom dimension registration applies to data processed from that point forward. Historic events keep the raw parameter but were never processed into the dimension.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Key events and conversions','exam','The team wants request submissions counted as the primary business outcome. What is the correct GA4 configuration?','Mark the generate_lead event as a key event in the property admin','Create a goal in the view settings','Add it to a custom report only','Rename the event to conversion','A','GA4 has no views or goals; an event is elevated by marking it a key event. That designation is what makes it available as a conversion metric across reports and Ads.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Key events and conversions','exam','A key event is marked today. What happens to the previous three months of the same event?','They are retroactively counted as key events','Key event designation applies from the moment it is set, so historic occurrences are not counted as key events','GA4 recomputes the last 30 days only','All historic data is deleted','B','Key event status is applied at processing time and is not backfilled. Comparisons across the change point must account for that boundary.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Key events and conversions','exam','Which counting method should be chosen for a request-for-quotation key event where each additional submission in a session has genuine commercial value?','Once per session','Once per user per day','Once per event, so every qualifying submission is counted','Once per property lifetime','C','Counting once per event records each occurrence, which is right when each occurrence carries value. Once per session would understate a buyer who submits several requests.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Key events and conversions','hard','GA4 reports 220 key events for a campaign while the CRM records 140 qualified leads from the same campaign and period. Which explanation is most likely and testable first?','GA4 is double counting sessions','GA4 attribution is broken','The CRM lost 80 records','GA4 counts every form submission including duplicates and unqualified entries, while the CRM counts after deduplication and qualification','D','The two systems count different populations at different points in the funnel. Reconciling deduplication and qualification rules explains most gaps of this shape before any bug is suspected.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Explorations','exam','An analyst must see the exact ordered sequence of steps buyers take before submitting a request, including where they drop. Which exploration technique fits?','Funnel exploration with the steps defined in order','Free form','Cohort exploration','User lifetime','A','Funnel exploration is built to express ordered steps and to report completion and abandonment at each. Free form cannot express step order.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Explorations','exam','Which exploration technique shows the paths users actually take after a chosen event, including unexpected routes?','Segment overlap','Path exploration','Funnel exploration','Cohort exploration','B','Path exploration is open ended and reveals the routes the analyst did not anticipate. A funnel can only report against the steps already defined.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Explorations','exam','A marketer wants to know how many users are both in the paid search segment and the submitted-a-request segment. Which technique answers this most directly?','User lifetime','Cohort exploration','Segment overlap','Funnel exploration','C','Segment overlap is designed to quantify intersections between two or three segments. The other techniques answer sequence, retention or value questions.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Explorations','hard','A free form exploration on a large date range shows a sampling notice. What is the correct professional response?','Report the numbers as exact','Ignore it because GA4 does not sample','Switch to Realtime','Narrow the date range or reduce cardinality, and state that the figures are estimates while the notice is present','D','GA4 explorations can sample above thresholds, so the notice means the figures are estimates. Reducing range or dimensionality restores an unsampled result.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Attribution','exam','Which attribution model does GA4 apply by default to key events in the standard reports?','Data-driven attribution, with direct-only journeys excluded from credit','Last click across all channels including direct','First click','Linear','A','GA4 defaults to data-driven attribution for eligible properties. Direct traffic is only credited when no other channel appears in the journey.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Attribution','exam','A campaign shows far more conversions in Google Ads than in GA4 for the same period. What is the most common structural cause?','GA4 has stopped collecting data','The two systems use different attribution models and conversion time bases, so counts diverge by design','Google Ads counts impressions as conversions','The GA4 property is filtered','B','Ads credits conversions to the click date under its own model, while GA4 reports on the conversion date under its model. That difference alone produces persistent gaps.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Attribution','exam','What does the acquisition report dimension Session default channel group describe?','The channel of the users very first session ever','The last channel touched in the last 90 days','The channel that started the session in which the activity occurred','The channel with the highest spend','C','Session-scoped channel describes the source of that particular session. First user channel is the separate user-scoped dimension.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Attribution','hard','A lookback window of 30 days is set for acquisition conversions. A buyer first clicked a paid advertisement 45 days before converting and clicked an organic result on day 2. How is credit assigned?','The paid click receives full credit','No credit is assigned to any channel','Credit is split evenly across both','The paid click falls outside the lookback window and receives no credit; eligible touches within the window share credit','D','Touches earlier than the lookback window are not eligible for credit. Only interactions inside the window enter the model.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Data collection and configuration','exam','A marketing site and a checkout application on different domains must be measured as one journey. What configuration is required?','Cross-domain measurement configured on the same data stream so the session and client identifier persist across domains','Two separate properties','A filter excluding one domain','A separate measurement identifier per domain','A','Cross-domain measurement preserves the client identifier across the domains, keeping a single session. Without it the second domain is recorded as a new referral session.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Data collection and configuration','exam','Internal staff traffic is inflating engagement metrics. What is the correct GA4 approach?','Delete the sessions afterwards','Define internal traffic by IP in the data stream and apply an internal traffic data filter','Ask staff not to visit the site','Set data retention to two months','B','GA4 identifies internal traffic through a rule on the stream and excludes it with a data filter. There is no facility to delete individual sessions after processing.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Data collection and configuration','exam','Why should a new data filter be set to testing mode before it is set to active?','Testing mode is required by Google policy','Testing mode collects more data','Active filters permanently exclude data with no way to recover it, whereas testing mode lets the effect be verified first','Filters cannot be changed once created','C','Excluded data is not recoverable, so an incorrect active filter destroys measurement. Testing mode tags the traffic so its scope can be checked before exclusion.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Data collection and configuration','hard','The default 14-month data retention has elapsed. Which reporting is affected?','All standard reports lose their history','Key event totals are deleted','Only Realtime is affected','Explorations and any user-level or event-level analysis beyond the retention window return no data, while aggregated standard reports remain','D','Retention governs user and event level data used by explorations. Aggregated standard reporting tables are unaffected by the setting.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Audiences','exam','A remarketing audience should contain users who submitted a request but never returned within 30 days. Which definition is correct?','Users with the generate_lead event, excluding those with any session in the following 30 days, with the membership duration set accordingly','All users who visited in 30 days','Users who viewed the pricing page','All users of the property','A','An audience is defined by inclusion and exclusion conditions over a stated window. The membership duration controls how long a qualifying user stays in the audience.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Audiences','exam','Are GA4 audiences populated retroactively when created?','Yes, over the full property history','GA4 can backfill a limited recent window for eligible audiences, but membership largely accrues from creation forward','No, never under any condition','Only for audiences based on demographics','B','Audience membership is primarily forward looking, with a limited backfill. Planning must allow time for an audience to fill before activation.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Reporting identity','exam','What does the blended reporting identity do in GA4?','Uses device identifier only','Disables all identity resolution','Uses user identifier where present, then device identifier, then modelled data to fill gaps','Uses only Google signals','C','Blended applies the identity hierarchy and adds modelling where identity is missing. Device-only ignores logged-in identity entirely.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Reporting identity','hard','Switching reporting identity from device-based to blended changes historic user counts in reports. Why is this not a data change?','The property was reprocessed','Blended adds new events','Historic data was deleted and recollected','Reporting identity is applied at query time, so the same underlying data is resolved differently without being altered','D','Identity space is a query-time setting in GA4, not a collection setting. The stored events are identical under either choice.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Events and parameters','exam','Which is the correct way to measure a single page application where content changes without a page load?','Disable enhanced measurement page changes and send page_view events on route change, or enable browser history based page views','Rely on automatic page_view only','Send a session_start on each route','Use a custom event named pageview','A','Route changes must be told to GA4 either by the history-based setting or an explicit page_view. Relying on load-time collection undercounts every subsequent screen.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Events and parameters','exam','What is the practical limit that matters when planning custom dimensions in a standard GA4 property?','There is no limit','There are per-property caps on registered event-scoped and user-scoped custom dimensions, so they must be planned rather than created ad hoc','Only one dimension is allowed','Limits apply only to metrics','B','Standard properties cap registered custom dimensions by scope. Creating them ad hoc exhausts the allocation and forces disruptive deletions later.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Explorations','exam','An exploration must exclude a specific internal test campaign. What is the correct mechanism inside the exploration?','A property level data filter','Deleting the campaign data','A segment or filter applied within the exploration on the campaign dimension','Changing the reporting identity','C','Explorations support segments and filters that shape the query without touching collected data. Property filters would exclude the data everywhere and permanently.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Attribution','hard','A marketer wants to prove that a new content programme creates demand rather than harvesting it. Which GA4 evidence is most persuasive?','Total sessions rising','A fall in bounce rate','A rise in key events overall','A rise in organic and direct sessions to the content, followed by a rise in branded search and assisted conversions in the model comparison','D','Demand creation appears as growth in upstream touches followed by downstream branded intent. Model comparison shows how credit shifts when upper-funnel touches are valued.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Data collection and configuration','exam','Which practice keeps a GA4 property compliant when collecting data from users in jurisdictions requiring consent?','Implement consent mode so tags adjust behaviour according to the granted consent state','Collect everything and delete on request','Disable analytics entirely','Rely on the browser to block tags','A','Consent mode communicates the consent state to the tags and adjusts collection accordingly. Post hoc deletion does not make the original collection lawful.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Reporting identity','exam','Why can the sum of users across channel rows exceed the total users figure in an acquisition report?','The report is faulty','A single user can appear in more than one channel row while being counted once in the unduplicated total','Users are being double collected','Sampling inflated the rows','B','User counts are unduplicated within each row and within the total, not additive across rows. A multi-channel user therefore appears more than once across the rows.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Key events and conversions','exam','A landing page test needs a single primary metric. Which is the most appropriate for a demand-side marketplace page?','Sessions','Average engagement time','Key event rate for request submission per session on that page','Scroll depth','C','The commercial outcome of the page is a submitted request, so the primary metric is the rate at which sessions produce one. Engagement measures are diagnostic, not primary.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Explorations','exam','In a funnel exploration, what does enabling the open funnel option change?','It removes all steps','It converts the funnel to a path exploration','It applies data-driven attribution','Users may enter the funnel at any step rather than being required to complete step one','D','An open funnel counts users entering at any step. A closed funnel requires entry at the first step, which is the correct choice for a strict sequence.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Audiences','hard','An audience defined as users who viewed pricing and did not submit a request is far smaller than expected. What is the most likely configuration cause?','The exclusion condition is set to permanently exclude on any future match rather than for a limited period, removing users who later converted','The audience needs a longer membership duration only','The property lacks Google signals','Audiences cannot use exclusions','A','GA4 exclusions can be temporary or permanent, and the permanent setting removes users retroactively on any match. That is the usual cause of a surprisingly small audience.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Data collection and configuration','exam','What is the effect of adding a measurement identifier to a second website without configuring cross-domain measurement?','Sessions continue seamlessly','A user moving between the sites is recorded with a new session attributed to a referral from the first site','The property rejects the second site','User identity merges automatically','B','Without cross-domain configuration the client identifier does not persist and the second site sees a referral. This inflates sessions and misattributes acquisition.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Events and parameters','exam','A marketer asks for the Arabic and English versions of a landing page to be compared. What is the cleanest measurement approach?','Compare two date ranges','Read the browser language in a spreadsheet','Send a language or page variant parameter with the page_view and key events, register it as a dimension, and compare the key event rate by variant','Create two GA4 properties','C','A parameter carried on the relevant events supports a direct comparison inside one property. Separate properties or date ranges introduce avoidable confounds.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Attribution','exam','What is the maximum practical use of the model comparison report?','To change historic data','To configure key events','To create audiences','To see how conversion credit by channel shifts under different attribution models before making a budget decision','D','Model comparison exposes how sensitive the channel picture is to the model chosen. That sensitivity is exactly what a budget decision needs to know.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Key events and conversions','hard','Key events fall 60% overnight with no change in sessions. Which check should come first?','Whether a recent site release changed the event name, the trigger or the tag placement, verified in DebugView and Realtime','Attribution settings','The data retention setting','Reporting identity','A','A step change in a single event with stable traffic points to instrumentation, not to demand. DebugView confirms in minutes whether the event still fires.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Explorations','exam','Which exploration best answers whether buyers acquired in March return and transact in the following weeks?','Path exploration','Cohort exploration with acquisition date as the cohort criterion','Segment overlap','Free form','B','Cohort exploration groups users by a common acquisition event and tracks their behaviour over subsequent periods. That is precisely the retention question asked.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Data collection and configuration','exam','Why should personally identifying information never be sent in GA4 event parameters?','It increases the event payload size','It cannot be registered as a dimension','Sending it breaches the terms of service and applicable data protection obligations, and can lead to data being purged','It slows down reporting','C','Google prohibits personal identifiers in Analytics and can delete affected data. The obligation also exists independently under data protection law.'),
('Google Analytics 4 Certification','Audiences','exam','What must be in place for a GA4 audience to be usable for remarketing in Google Ads?','Only the audience definition','A funnel exploration','A key event marked','A linked Google Ads account, the necessary consent and signals settings, and an audience that meets the minimum size for serving','D','Activation requires the account link and the consent basis, and serving requires the audience to reach the minimum size. Definition alone does not make an audience usable.')
) as v(certification, syllabus_area, difficulty, question, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_option, rationale)
where not exists (select 1 from public.certification_exam_question where certification = 'Google Analytics 4 Certification');

-- ============================================================================
-- CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional) — Digital Marketing Institute — 40 questions
-- ============================================================================
insert into public.certification_exam_question
  (certification, syllabus_area, difficulty, question, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_option, rationale)
select * from (values
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Digital Marketing Strategy and Planning','exam','A B2B marketplace has AED 15,000 a month in total media budget and a target of 150 qualified requests. What must the plan state to be actionable?','A maximum allowable cost per qualified request, the assumed conversion rate at each stage and the volume each channel must deliver','The list of channels to be used','The creative concept','The agency roster','A','A plan becomes actionable when volume, conversion and allowable cost are stated together. Channel and creative choices follow from those numbers rather than preceding them.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Digital Marketing Strategy and Planning','exam','Which sequence correctly orders the stages of a digital marketing plan?','Tactics, objectives, situation analysis, control','Situation analysis, objectives, strategy, tactics, action, control','Objectives, control, tactics, situation analysis','Creative, media, measurement, objectives','B','Planning frameworks such as SOSTAC run from where the business is, to what it must achieve, to how and with what, and finally to control. Starting with tactics leaves the objective unstated.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Digital Marketing Strategy and Planning','hard','Two channels each report a cost per lead of AED 90. Channel A leads close at 4%, channel B at 11%. What is the correct decision basis?','Both channels are equally efficient','Channel A should be preferred for its larger volume','Cost per closed deal, which is materially lower for channel B, should govern allocation','Cost per click should be used instead','C','Cost per lead ignores what happens after the lead. Dividing by close rate converts both to cost per closed deal, which is the figure the business pays from.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Search Engine Optimisation','exam','A category page ranks on page three for a high-value procurement term. Which action is most likely to move it first?','Publish twenty new unrelated blog posts','Change the domain name','Buy more backlinks from directories','Improve the pages match to search intent, strengthen internal links to it from relevant pages and resolve any indexation or speed issues','D','A page already ranking has recognised relevance, so intent match, internal linking and technical health give the fastest gains. Unrelated volume and paid directory links do not address the specific page.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Search Engine Optimisation','exam','Two language versions of the same page exist in Arabic and English. What technical signal should be implemented?','Hreflang annotations declaring the language and region of each version, each self-referencing and reciprocal','A canonical tag pointing both to the English page','Robots noindex on the Arabic version','A redirect from Arabic to English','A','Hreflang tells the search engine which version to serve to which audience. Canonicalising or redirecting one language removes it from search entirely.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Search Engine Optimisation','exam','What distinguishes an informational keyword from a transactional one in a B2B context, and why does it matter for planning?','Only word length distinguishes them','Informational terms indicate research and suit content, while transactional terms indicate readiness to buy and suit landing pages and paid search','Informational terms always have higher volume','The distinction only applies to consumer markets','B','Intent determines which asset should rank and what the page should ask the visitor to do. Aiming a quotation form at a research query wastes the visit.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Search Engine Optimisation','hard','Organic sessions fall 35% after a site migration while rankings for the same terms are stable in the tracking tool. What should be checked first?','Content quality','Backlink quantity','Whether redirects, canonical tags and the sitemap map old URLs to new ones, and whether tracking still fires on the new templates','Domain authority','C','A stable ranking with lost sessions points at either lost URL mapping or lost measurement. Both are checked before any content hypothesis.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Paid Search','exam','A small-budget account is spending 60% of its budget on broad match terms with a 0.4% conversion rate. What is the appropriate first action?','Increase the daily budget','Raise bids across the account','Pause the whole account','Add negative keywords and tighten match types so budget concentrates on qualified intent','D','Small budgets must be protected from irrelevant queries before anything else. Negatives and match type control redirect the same money to qualified intent.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Paid Search','exam','What does a high impression share lost to rank indicate?','Ad rank is too low, driven by bid, expected click-through rate, ad relevance or landing page experience','The budget is exhausted','The keyword has no volume','The account is disapproved','A','Loss to rank is an eligibility problem rather than a funding one. It is addressed through the quality components and the bid, not by adding budget.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Paid Search','hard','A campaign has 60 conversions in 30 days. The team wants to move from manual bidding to a value-based automated strategy. What is the professional judgement?','Switch immediately, automation always outperforms','Conversion volume is at the low end for reliable learning, so a target-based strategy should be introduced carefully with realistic targets and a learning period allowed','Automation cannot be used below 500 conversions under any circumstance','Manual bidding should never be replaced','B','Automated strategies need sufficient conversion signal to learn, and 60 in 30 days is marginal. Introducing it with realistic targets and tolerating a learning period is the defensible middle course.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Social Media Marketing','exam','Which objective and format pairing is most appropriate for reaching procurement decision makers on a professional network with a limited budget?','Reach objective with a video view campaign','Brand awareness with broad geographic targeting','Lead generation objective with an in-platform form targeted by job function and company size','Engagement objective on a consumer network','C','Function and firm size targeting reaches the buying centre precisely, and an in-platform form removes post-click friction. Broad reach objectives spend the budget on the wrong people.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Social Media Marketing','exam','An organic social account posts daily but generates almost no site visits. What diagnosis is most useful?','The posting frequency is too low','The brand needs a new logo','The platform algorithm is broken','The content is not matched to an audience need or does not contain a reason and a route to visit, so engagement does not convert into traffic','D','Traffic requires both relevance and an explicit route. Frequency without a reason to click produces engagement that stops on the platform.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Social Media Marketing','exam','What is the primary purpose of a social media content calendar in a small team?','To align content with campaign objectives and resources in advance, so production is planned rather than reactive','To increase the number of posts','To satisfy the platform algorithm','To replace performance reporting','A','A calendar is a resource and alignment instrument, tying output to objectives and capacity. It does not by itself increase performance.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Content Marketing','exam','Which content asset best serves a procurement manager in the consideration stage of a B2B purchase?','A brand manifesto video','A comparison guide setting out selection criteria, typical costs and risks for the category','A recruitment page','A general company newsletter','B','Consideration-stage buyers are building selection criteria and need decision support. Brand and corporate content does not help them evaluate.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Content Marketing','exam','A content programme is measured only by page views. What is the main weakness?','Page views are difficult to collect','Page views are not available in analytics','Page views do not indicate whether the content moved anyone toward a commercial outcome, so the programme cannot be optimised','Page views penalise long articles','C','A volume metric with no link to outcome cannot guide investment. Assisted conversions, qualified leads and pipeline influence make the programme steerable.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Content Marketing','hard','A bilingual content programme publishes English first and translates to Arabic two weeks later. Arabic performance is consistently weak. Which explanation deserves testing first?','Arabic audiences read less','Arabic content should be discontinued','The content management system cannot render Arabic','Translated content lags the news cycle and is not adapted to the search terms and examples the Arabic audience actually uses','D','Delayed translation loses timeliness and, more importantly, keyword and cultural fit. Native keyword research and adaptation is the standard remedy before any conclusion about the audience.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Email Marketing','exam','A nurture sequence has a 38% open rate but a 0.6% click rate. Where does the problem most likely lie?','The body content and call to action, since the opens show the subject line is working','The subject lines','The sending domain reputation','The list size','A','A strong open with a weak click isolates the failure inside the message. Subject line and deliverability are already demonstrated to be working.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Email Marketing','exam','What is the effect of continuing to email a segment that has not opened in twelve months?','It increases total reach at no cost','It damages sender reputation and deliverability for the whole list, reducing inbox placement for engaged recipients','It has no effect on deliverability','It improves the open rate','B','Mailbox providers weigh engagement signals at the domain level. Persistently unengaged recipients drag down placement for everyone else.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Email Marketing','exam','Which email marketing practice is required rather than optional under a consent-based regime?','Personalising the first name','Sending at a fixed time of day','A clear identification of the sender and a working unsubscribe mechanism honoured promptly','Including images in every message','C','Sender identification and a functioning opt-out are legal requirements in consent-based regimes. Personalisation and design choices are optimisation, not compliance.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Display and Video Advertising','exam','A display campaign delivers a 0.06% click-through rate and no conversions after AED 6,000. What is the most defensible action for a small-budget advertiser?','Increase the display budget to gain scale','Extend the campaign for another month','Change the banner colours','Stop the broad display spend and redeploy to channels with demonstrated qualified intent, retaining only a retargeting audience','D','A small budget cannot absorb a channel with no demonstrated outcome. Retargeting is retained because it addresses an audience with proven interest.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Display and Video Advertising','exam','What is the correct definition of viewability as used in display measurement?','An impression meeting the minimum pixel and duration thresholds for having had the opportunity to be seen','Any impression served','An impression that was clicked','An impression that led to a conversion','A','Viewability measures the opportunity to see against defined pixel and time thresholds. It is neither delivery alone nor any measure of response.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Display and Video Advertising','hard','A retargeting campaign reports a 9% conversion rate against 0.8% for prospecting, and the team proposes moving all budget to retargeting. What is the flaw?','Retargeting numbers are always inflated by fraud','Retargeting can only convert an audience that prospecting created, so removing prospecting shrinks the pool it depends on','Conversion rates cannot be compared','Prospecting is more efficient by definition','B','Retargeting harvests demand that upper-funnel activity generated. Cutting the source starves the retargeting pool within weeks.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Website Optimisation','exam','A landing page converts at 1.2%. Which change should be tested first on a demand-side B2B page?','The footer links','The favicon','The match between the advertisement promise and the page headline and offer, together with the number of required form fields','The colour of the privacy notice','C','Message match and form friction are the two largest and most repeatable levers on a lead-generation page. Peripheral elements rarely move the outcome.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Website Optimisation','exam','Why does mobile page load time matter commercially for a paid traffic landing page?','It affects the server bill','It only affects organic search','It changes the ad auction rules','Visitors abandon before the page renders, so slow pages waste the media already paid for and depress the conversion rate','D','Every abandoned load is media already purchased and lost. Speed therefore acts directly on the effective cost per acquisition.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Website Optimisation','hard','A test moves conversion from 2.0% to 2.4% with 1,100 sessions per arm and a p-value of 0.31. What should be reported?','The result is not statistically distinguishable from no effect at this sample size and should not be implemented as a proven win','A 20% uplift has been achieved','The test proves the change is harmful','Statistical significance is irrelevant for small budgets','A','A p-value of 0.31 means the observed difference is well within what chance produces. Reporting it as an uplift would put a false number into the plan.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Analytics','exam','Which metric set best describes the health of a demand-side marketplace funnel?','Sessions, bounce rate and time on page','Sessions, landing page conversion rate to request, qualified request rate, cost per qualified request and close rate','Impressions and reach','Followers and engagement rate','B','A funnel is described by the rate at each stage and the cost of the outcome. Traffic and engagement metrics do not describe commercial progression.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Analytics','exam','A dashboard shows a rise in total conversions while cost per acquisition also rises. What is the correct reading?','Performance improved','The data is contradictory','Volume was bought at a worse rate, so the change is only beneficial if the extra volume remains profitable at the new cost','Cost per acquisition is not a valid metric','C','Volume and efficiency can move in opposite directions. The decision depends on whether the marginal acquisitions still clear the allowable cost.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Analytics','hard','Marketing reports 400 leads; sales reports 120. Both are confident. What is the professional resolution?','Average the two numbers','Stop reporting lead counts','Use the marketing number externally','Agree a single definition of a lead with the qualification criteria and the system of record, then report both raw and qualified counts against it','D','The gap is almost always definitional rather than a data fault. A shared definition with a named system of record ends the dispute permanently.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Digital Marketing Strategy and Planning','exam','What is the purpose of a buyer persona in a B2B digital plan?','To capture the roles, criteria, objections and information sources of the people in the buying centre so content and targeting can address them','To describe the ideal employee','To set the media budget','To replace market sizing','A','Personas encode who decides and on what basis, which is what targeting and content need. They do not substitute for sizing or budgeting.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Digital Marketing Strategy and Planning','exam','A quarterly plan sets a target of 150 qualified requests but historic data shows a maximum of 60. What should the planner do?','Publish the target unchanged','State the gap explicitly, set out what would have to change in traffic, conversion or budget to close it, and agree a realistic target','Remove the target','Blame the sales team','B','A target with no route is a wish rather than a plan. Quantifying the gap converts it into a decision about resources.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Social Media Marketing','hard','A social campaign in Arabic uses right-to-left copy laid over creative designed for left-to-right reading. Performance is poor. What is the underlying issue?','Arabic copy is inherently less persuasive','The platform does not support Arabic','The visual hierarchy and the reading order conflict, so the offer and call to action are not encountered in the intended sequence','The budget was too low','C','Layout and reading direction must agree or the message is read out of order. Creative for Arabic needs the composition mirrored, not only the words translated.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Email Marketing','exam','What is the correct role of a double opt-in in a B2B email programme?','It increases list size','It is required for all transactional email','It removes the need for an unsubscribe link','It confirms the address and the intent, improving deliverability and creating a defensible consent record at the cost of some list growth','D','Confirmation trades raw volume for verified addresses and evidence of consent. Transactional messages sit under a different basis entirely.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Paid Search','exam','What is the practical purpose of a dedicated landing page for each paid search ad group?','It allows the page message to match the query and ad, which raises both conversion rate and ad relevance','It reduces the media cost directly','It removes the need for negative keywords','It improves organic ranking','A','Message match across query, advertisement and page lifts conversion and feeds back into quality signals. It does not substitute for query control.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Content Marketing','exam','How should a small team decide which content to produce next?','Produce whatever the team finds interesting','Rank candidate topics by search demand, buyer relevance and effort, then produce the highest ranked','Copy the competitor content calendar','Produce one asset per channel each week','B','A ranked backlog on demand, relevance and effort spends limited production capacity where it returns most. Imitation and quotas ignore both demand and cost.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Website Optimisation','exam','Which form design change is most likely to raise completion for a B2B quotation request?','Adding more explanatory text','Adding a captcha to every field','Reducing the required fields to those needed to route the request, deferring the rest to a later stage','Splitting the form across six pages','C','Every required field costs completions, so only routing-critical fields belong at first submission. Additional friction or length works in the wrong direction.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Analytics','exam','A marketer wants to attribute pipeline to marketing activity. What is required beyond analytics tags?','Nothing further','A larger media budget','More conversion events','A closed loop that passes the source of each lead into the customer record and returns the outcome, so pipeline and revenue can be reported by source','D','Analytics ends at the site boundary, so source data must travel with the lead into the sales system. Without that return path pipeline cannot be attributed.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Display and Video Advertising','exam','What is frequency capping for and when does it matter most?','To limit repeated exposure to the same user, which protects a small budget from spending disproportionately on a narrow audience','To increase reach on a large budget','To lower the creative production cost','To improve viewability thresholds','A','Capping spreads a limited budget across more of the intended audience. On a narrow B2B audience without a cap, spend concentrates on a few users.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Search Engine Optimisation','exam','What is the relationship between paid search and organic search in a small-budget plan?','They are interchangeable and only one should be used','Paid delivers immediate qualified traffic while organic compounds slowly, so paid covers the near term while organic is built for durable cost per lead','Organic results can be purchased directly','Paid search improves organic rankings','B','The two differ in speed and in the durability of their cost structure. Running paid while building organic is the standard resolution on a small budget.'),
('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Digital Marketing Strategy and Planning','hard','A CEO asks for the single number that shows whether digital marketing is working for a marketplace. Which answer is most professional?','Total website sessions','Total impressions','The cost per qualified request compared with the gross profit of a converted request, since it states both efficiency and whether the activity pays','Follower growth','C','A single defensible number must relate cost to the value it produces. Traffic and audience measures cannot show whether the activity pays.')
,('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)','Website Optimisation','hard','A landing page test needs 1,900 sessions per variation to detect the target uplift, but the page receives 700 sessions a month in total. What is the professional course of action?','Run the test for two weeks and report whichever variation is ahead','Lower the confidence level to 80% so a result appears sooner','Split the traffic across four variations to gather more information','Accept that a reliable A/B result is months away, and instead make a larger evidence-based change to the page while monitoring the conversion rate against its prior range','D','At this volume the required sample cannot be reached in a usable timeframe, and reading early or weakening the threshold manufactures false wins. A larger, research-backed change monitored against the historic range is the honest alternative.')
) as v(certification, syllabus_area, difficulty, question, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_option, rationale)
where not exists (select 1 from public.certification_exam_question where certification = 'CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)');

-- ============================================================================
-- Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate (Meta) — 40 questions
-- ============================================================================
insert into public.certification_exam_question
  (certification, syllabus_area, difficulty, question, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_option, rationale)
select * from (values
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Campaign objectives','exam','A B2B marketplace wants procurement managers to submit a request on its own website. Which campaign objective should be selected?','Leads, optimising for the website conversion event that records a submitted request','Awareness','Engagement','Traffic','A','The objective tells delivery what outcome to seek, so it must name the event the business actually values. Traffic and engagement optimise for cheaper, less valuable actions.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Campaign objectives','exam','What is the consequence of choosing the Traffic objective when the business goal is website conversions?','Delivery is unchanged','Delivery optimises for people likely to click rather than to convert, usually producing cheaper clicks and a worse cost per conversion','Conversions cannot be tracked','The campaign will be rejected','B','Optimisation follows the objective, so the system finds click-prone rather than conversion-prone people. The click metric improves while the business metric worsens.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Campaign objectives','exam','Which objective is appropriate when the goal is to collect contact details without sending the user off platform?','Sales','Awareness','Leads with an instant form','App promotion','C','An instant form keeps the user in the app and removes the load and navigation friction of an external landing page. It is the native answer to off-platform drop-off.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Campaign objectives','hard','A campaign optimising for a conversion event exits the learning phase only rarely and costs are volatile. The event occurs about 12 times a week per ad set. What is the correct remedy?','Add more ad sets to spread the budget','Change the creative daily','Reduce the budget','Consolidate ad sets and optimise for a higher-volume event higher in the funnel, or use the conversions API with value rules, so the ad set can accumulate enough events to stabilise','D','Learning requires roughly fifty optimisation events per ad set per week. Consolidating and moving to a higher-volume event supplies that signal; fragmenting makes it worse.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Advantage+ and automation','exam','What does Advantage+ audience change about how an ad set is targeted?','It treats the supplied audience information as a suggestion and allows delivery to find qualifying people beyond it','It removes targeting entirely','It restricts delivery to a saved audience','It applies only to catalogue campaigns','A','Advantage+ audience uses the provided signals as a starting point and expands where performance warrants. It is a broadening mechanism, not a removal of intent.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Advantage+ and automation','exam','Advantage+ placements is recommended for most campaigns. Why?','It reduces the number of creatives needed','It lets delivery allocate impressions across every eligible surface at the lowest available cost for the chosen outcome','It guarantees placement on Feed only','It removes the need for a conversion event','B','Opening placements enlarges the auction pool so the system can buy the same outcome more cheaply. Restricting placements narrows supply and usually raises cost.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Advantage+ and automation','exam','What does Advantage campaign budget do?','Sets a fixed budget per ad set','Caps the cost per result','Distributes one campaign budget dynamically across ad sets toward the best performing opportunities','Disables automatic bidding','C','Campaign budget optimisation moves money between ad sets in flight based on observed opportunity. It is a distribution mechanism, not a cost cap.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Advantage+ and automation','hard','An advertiser applies Advantage campaign budget across ad sets with very different audience sizes and value. Spend collects almost entirely in one ad set. What is the professional interpretation?','The feature is malfunctioning','Advantage campaign budget should never be used','The budget should be reduced','The system is behaving as designed by chasing the cheapest results, so if the starved ad sets are strategically necessary they require their own campaigns or minimum spend controls','D','Budget optimisation maximises results at lowest cost and is indifferent to strategic intent. Strategic guarantees must be expressed structurally, through separate campaigns or spend limits.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Audiences','exam','Which audience type is built from a list of existing supplier contacts uploaded by the advertiser?','Custom audience from a customer list','Lookalike audience','Saved audience','Advantage+ audience','A','A customer list upload creates a custom audience matched against platform users. A lookalike is then modelled from it.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Audiences','exam','An advertiser creates a 1% lookalike and a 10% lookalike from the same source. What is the trade-off?','The 10% is always better','The 1% is closer to the source and typically converts better at smaller scale, while the 10% reaches far more people with weaker similarity','They are identical in behaviour','The 1% reaches more people','B','Lookalike percentage sets the similarity threshold and therefore the size. Precision and scale move in opposite directions across that range.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Audiences','exam','What is the minimum practical requirement for a source audience used to build a lookalike?','One person','Ten thousand people exactly','A source of at least the platform minimum, of sufficient quality, drawn from the country being targeted','It must be a website audience','C','Lookalike modelling needs a source meeting the platform minimum and drawn from the target country. Source quality determines the value of everything modelled from it.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Audiences','hard','Two ad sets in the same campaign target overlapping custom audiences. Results are worse than when one ad set ran alone. What is the mechanism?','The platform penalises duplicate audiences','Overlap improves frequency and always helps','The creative was rejected','Audience fragmentation and auction overlap split the learning signal and can raise costs as the advertiser competes for the same people','D','Splitting one audience across ad sets divides the events each needs to learn from. It can also place the advertiser in the auction against itself.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Measurement','exam','What is the role of the Meta Pixel on an advertiser website?','It records visitor actions and reports them as events, enabling conversion optimisation, attribution and website custom audiences','It hosts the landing page','It blocks competitors from advertising','It creates lookalike audiences without any source','A','The pixel is the measurement and signal layer connecting site behaviour to delivery. Optimisation, attribution and site audiences all depend on it.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Measurement','exam','Why would an advertiser implement the Conversions API in addition to the pixel?','To replace campaign objectives','To send events server side so that signal lost to browser restrictions is recovered, improving optimisation and reported attribution','To reduce the ad budget','To create instant forms','B','Browser-side collection is degraded by tracking restrictions, and a server-side channel restores the missing events. Better signal directly improves delivery decisions.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Measurement','hard','With both the pixel and the Conversions API sending the same conversion, what must be configured?','Nothing, duplicates are acceptable','A second pixel','Event deduplication using a shared event identifier so a single conversion is not counted twice','Separate ad accounts','C','A shared event id lets the platform recognise the two reports as one conversion. Without it, reported results and optimisation signal are both inflated.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Measurement','hard','Ads Manager reports 90 leads while the advertiser CRM records 55 for the same period. Which explanation should be examined first?','Ads Manager is inflating results deliberately','The CRM deleted records','The pixel is not installed','Different attribution windows and models, plus form submissions the CRM rejects as unqualified or duplicate, explain most of a gap of this shape','D','Platform attribution counts conversions within its own window and model; the CRM counts qualified records. Reconciling windows and qualification usually accounts for the difference.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Measurement','exam','What does the default attribution setting of seven-day click and one-day view mean?','A conversion is credited if it occurs within seven days of a click or one day of a view of the advertisement','Only clicks are counted','Views are counted for seven days','Conversions are credited indefinitely','A','The setting defines the eligible window separately for clicks and for views. Any conversion outside those windows is not credited to the advertisement.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Measurement','exam','Which reporting breakdown best identifies whether an Arabic or English creative is driving results?','Age and gender','A breakdown by ad, where each language creative is a separate ad, supported by consistent naming','Placement only','Device only','B','Language performance is read at the creative level, so each language must be its own ad. Demographic and placement breakdowns cannot separate them.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Creative and formats','exam','A single advertisement must present six supplier categories. Which format is designed for this?','Single image','Instant form only','Carousel','Story poll','C','A carousel presents multiple cards each with its own image and link. A single image cannot separate six offers.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Creative and formats','exam','Why should creative be produced in both 1:1 or 4:5 and 9:16 aspect ratios?','To satisfy the file size limits','Because the platform rejects square images','To lower the cost per thousand impressions','Because feed and vertical full-screen surfaces have different shapes, and cropped creative loses the message on one of them','D','Different placements render different aspect ratios, and automatic cropping can cut the offer or the logo. Producing for both preserves the message everywhere.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Creative and formats','exam','What is the recommended practice for text in advertisement images?','Keep on-image text limited and carry the detail in the primary text, since heavy text reduces legibility and can affect delivery','Fill the image with text for clarity','Use no text at all under any circumstance','Use the same text as the headline','A','Dense on-image text is hard to read on mobile and historically affects delivery. The primary text field is where detail belongs.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Creative and formats','hard','A team wants to test five creatives fairly within one ad set on a small budget. What is the professional judgement?','Run all five and pick the winner after two days','A small budget across five creatives leaves each with too little delivery to distinguish, so test two or three at a time with enough budget for the system to allocate meaningfully','Use dynamic creative with fifty assets','Run each creative in its own campaign','B','Delivery is allocated unevenly and a small budget cannot give five variants meaningful exposure. Fewer variants with adequate budget produce a readable result.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Creative and formats','exam','What does Advantage+ creative do to a submitted asset?','It replaces the asset with a stock image','It translates the copy into every language','It applies automatic enhancements and per-person variations such as cropping, brightness or text arrangement to improve performance','It converts images into video only','C','Advantage+ creative varies presentation per person within the supplied assets. It does not source new assets or translate copy.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Campaign structure','exam','At which level are the audience, placements, budget and schedule defined?','Campaign','Account','Ad','Ad set','D','The ad set holds targeting, placements, budget and schedule. Objective sits at campaign level and creative at ad level.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Campaign structure','exam','An advertiser edits the audience of an ad set that is performing well and has exited learning. What should be expected?','A significant edit resets the ad set into the learning phase, with unstable performance until enough events accumulate again','No change to delivery','The ad set is deleted','The budget is refunded','A','Significant edits reset learning because the delivery model must relearn. Frequent edits keep an ad set permanently unstable.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Campaign structure','exam','What is the difference between a daily budget and a lifetime budget?','There is none','A daily budget paces spend to an average per day, while a lifetime budget spends a total over the schedule with pacing free to vary by day','Lifetime budgets cannot use scheduling','Daily budgets cannot be edited','B','Daily budgets pace to a per-day average; lifetime budgets pace to a total across the flight. Lifetime is what enables day-part scheduling.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Campaign structure','hard','A small advertiser runs six campaigns each with four ad sets on AED 15,000 a month. Results are volatile and cost per lead is high. What is the first structural fix?','Increase the budget tenfold','Add more creatives per ad set','Consolidate into far fewer campaigns and ad sets so each accumulates enough conversion events to leave the learning phase','Switch to the awareness objective','C','Twenty-four ad sets on this budget leaves each far below the events needed to learn. Consolidation is the standard remedy before any budget argument.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Business tools','exam','Which asset must own the pixel, pages and ad accounts so that access survives staff changes?','A personal profile','The agency personal account','A shared password','A Meta Business Manager or Business Portfolio owning the assets, with people assigned roles against them','D','Assets owned by a business portfolio persist independently of any individual. Personal ownership makes the assets hostage to one person.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Business tools','exam','An agency needs to run advertisements for a client without owning the client assets. What is the correct arrangement?','The client grants the agency partner access to the specific assets through their business portfolio','The client shares login credentials','The agency creates a duplicate pixel','The agency uses a personal profile','A','Partner access grants scoped, revocable permissions on the client owned assets. Credential sharing is insecure and breaches platform terms.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Business tools','exam','What is the purpose of domain verification?','It speeds up page loading','It establishes the advertiser authority over the domain and is required to configure and prioritise web conversion events','It creates a custom audience','It removes the need for a pixel','B','Verification proves control of the domain, which the platform requires before web event configuration. It has no effect on site performance.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Business tools','hard','After configuring web events, an advertiser finds that a newly added conversion event does not optimise as expected. Which check is most relevant?','The creative aspect ratio','The campaign name','Whether the event is included and correctly prioritised in the aggregated event configuration for the verified domain','The billing country','C','Web events must be configured and ranked for the domain before they can be optimised toward. An unranked event will not drive delivery.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Policy and compliance','exam','An advertisement for a marketplace states a guaranteed saving that the advertiser cannot substantiate. What is the correct action?','Run it and see whether it is rejected','Run it only in one country','Add small print in the image','Remove the unsubstantiated claim, since advertising policy and consumer protection both require claims to be accurate and supportable','D','Claims must be accurate and capable of substantiation under both platform policy and consumer law. Disclaimers do not rescue an unsupportable claim.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Policy and compliance','exam','A campaign uploads a customer list for a custom audience. What is the advertiser obligation?','The advertiser must have a lawful basis and the necessary consent or notice for using those contacts for advertising, and must honour objections','None, the platform assumes responsibility','Only that the file is correctly formatted','Only that the list is at least 1,000 rows','A','The advertiser remains the controller of the uploaded personal data and must hold a lawful basis. File formatting is a technical detail, not the obligation.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Policy and compliance','exam','What happens if an advertisement is rejected for policy reasons?','The account is permanently closed','The advertisement can be edited to comply and resubmitted, or a review can be requested if the advertiser believes the decision is wrong','The budget is forfeited','The pixel stops collecting','B','Rejection applies to the advertisement and allows edit and resubmission or an appeal. It does not by itself close the account or forfeit budget.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Measurement','exam','Which is the correct definition of frequency in Ads Manager?','The number of times an advertisement was clicked','The number of ad sets running','The average number of times each person reached saw the advertisement in the reporting period','The number of days the campaign ran','C','Frequency is impressions divided by people reached. It measures repetition per person, not clicks or duration.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Measurement','hard','A campaign shows rising frequency and falling click-through rate over three weeks with a fixed audience. What is the standard interpretation and response?','The audience is too large; narrow it','The objective is wrong','The budget must be doubled','Creative fatigue within a narrow audience, addressed by refreshing creative or expanding the audience','D','Repetition on a fixed audience degrades response over time. New creative or a larger pool restores it.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Campaign objectives','hard','Which optimisation setting should be chosen when the advertiser cares that leads are genuine rather than merely numerous, using an instant form?','Higher intent, which adds a review step to the form at the cost of some volume','More volume','Reach','Link clicks','A','The higher intent form adds a confirmation step that filters accidental submissions. It trades volume for quality, which is the stated preference.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Audiences','exam','What is a website custom audience built from?','A manually uploaded spreadsheet','Pixel or Conversions API events describing visitor behaviour on the advertiser site, within a stated retention window','Page followers only','Lookalike modelling','B','Website custom audiences are assembled from measured site events over a retention window. Uploaded lists and page engagement are different source types.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Advantage+ and automation','exam','When is it defensible to restrict placements manually rather than use Advantage+ placements?','Whenever costs rise','Always, for greater control','When the creative genuinely cannot render acceptably on a surface or a documented brand safety requirement excludes it, accepting the higher cost','Only for lead campaigns','C','Restriction is defensible when a creative or policy constraint is real, and it carries a known cost. Restricting for a general sense of control raises cost with no benefit.'),
('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate','Campaign structure','exam','What is the correct use of a campaign spending limit?','To pace daily delivery','To exit the learning phase','To set the bid','To cap the total a campaign can spend as a control against overspend, independent of daily pacing','D','A spending limit is a hard ceiling on cumulative campaign spend. Pacing and bidding are governed by separate settings.')
) as v(certification, syllabus_area, difficulty, question, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_option, rationale)
where not exists (select 1 from public.certification_exam_question where certification = 'Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate');

-- ============================================================================
-- Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design (Adobe) — 40 questions
-- ============================================================================
insert into public.certification_exam_question
  (certification, syllabus_area, difficulty, question, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_option, rationale)
select * from (values
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Working in the design industry','exam','A client brief for a bilingual marketplace campaign lists no measurable outcome. What should the designer do before starting production?','Agree the purpose, audience, deliverable specifications and success criteria in writing, and confirm the scope and review rounds','Begin design and ask later','Assume the previous campaign requirements apply','Produce three concepts to prompt a reaction','A','Requirements gathering precedes production because the deliverable specification determines every later decision. Written agreement also fixes scope and revision expectations.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Working in the design industry','exam','A designer wants to use a photograph found through an image search in a paid advertisement. What is the correct position?','Any image online may be used with attribution','A licence permitting commercial use must be obtained, and the licence terms and any model or property releases must be respected','Images may be used if modified by 30%','Attribution removes the need for a licence','B','Commercial use requires a licence granting it, plus releases where identifiable people or property appear. Attribution and modification do not create a right to use.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Working in the design industry','exam','Which file should be delivered to a client who needs to make future text edits to a poster?','A flattened JPEG','A screenshot','The layered working file together with the linked assets and fonts as licensing permits, plus a print-ready PDF','A PNG at screen resolution','C','Editability requires the layered source and its dependencies. Flattened formats are outputs and cannot be edited back into a working state.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Working in the design industry','hard','A client requests a design that closely imitates a competitor identity to benefit from the association. How should the designer respond?','Produce it, since layout cannot be protected','Produce it and add a disclaimer','Produce it with small changes to colours','Decline the imitation and propose a distinct direction, explaining the trademark and passing-off risk to the client','D','Deliberate imitation of an identity creates trademark and passing-off exposure for the client and the designer. The professional response is to name the risk and offer a lawful alternative.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Project requirements and setup','exam','A campaign asset must appear on a billboard and on a mobile advertisement. What is the correct production approach?','Design with vector elements and high-resolution imagery, then produce separate compositions sized and simplified for each medium','Design once at screen size and enlarge','Design at billboard size and shrink for mobile without changes','Use the same JPEG for both','A','Enlarging raster work degrades it, and a billboard composition is unreadable when reduced. Each medium needs its own composition from scalable sources.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Project requirements and setup','exam','What colour mode and resolution should be set for a document destined for commercial offset printing?','RGB at 72 pixels per inch','CMYK at 300 pixels per inch at final size, with bleed applied','Grayscale at 150 pixels per inch','Indexed colour at 96 pixels per inch','B','Offset presses print in CMYK inks and require sufficient resolution at final size plus bleed for trimming. Screen settings produce colour shifts and soft output.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Project requirements and setup','exam','Why is bleed added to a print document?','To increase the ink coverage','To improve the resolution','So that artwork intended to reach the edge extends beyond the trim line, preventing white slivers when the sheet is cut','To create a margin for text','C','Cutting has a mechanical tolerance, so artwork must extend past the trim. Bleed is unrelated to resolution or to the safe text margin.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Project requirements and setup','hard','A photograph supplied by the client is 900 by 600 pixels and must fill an A3 poster. What is the professional response?','Upscale it and sharpen heavily','Convert it to a vector automatically','Print at 72 pixels per inch','Explain that the file lacks the resolution for A3 at print quality and request a larger original, or redesign so the image is used at a size it supports','D','A3 at print resolution needs several times that pixel count, and interpolation cannot create detail. Either a better source or a different composition is required.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Design principles','exam','A landing page hero has the headline, an image, a paragraph and a button all at similar visual weight. Which principle is being violated and what is the fix?','Hierarchy; establish a dominant element and rank the rest by size, weight, colour and space so the eye is led in the intended order','Repetition; add more elements','Alignment; centre everything','Proximity; increase all spacing equally','A','Equal weight leaves no entry point and the viewer must search. Hierarchy is created by deliberate contrast in size, weight, colour and space.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Design principles','exam','What does the principle of proximity govern?','The distance from the viewer to the screen','That elements placed close together are perceived as related, so grouping communicates relationship before any label does','The resolution of images','The number of typefaces used','B','Proximity is a grouping cue read pre-attentively. Spacing therefore communicates structure faster than headings or labels.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Design principles','exam','A layout uses six different alignments across the page. What is the likely effect and the remedy?','It appears dynamic; keep it','It improves accessibility; keep it','It reads as disorganised; establish a grid and align elements to a small number of consistent edges','It has no perceptible effect','C','Multiple arbitrary edges read as carelessness and slow scanning. A grid with few consistent alignments produces order without rigidity.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Design principles','hard','A bilingual campaign must present the same layout in English and Arabic. Which adaptation is required beyond translating the words?','Only the font needs changing','Arabic must be set in the same point size as English in every case','Nothing beyond the text','The composition must be mirrored so that the reading order, visual hierarchy and the position of the call to action follow right-to-left reading','D','Reading direction determines the order in which a composition is scanned, so the layout must be mirrored, not only translated. Arabic type also usually needs its own size and leading to match optical weight.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Design principles','exam','Which use of white space is professionally correct?','White space is an active element that separates groups, creates emphasis and improves legibility','White space is wasted area and should be filled','White space must always be equal on all sides','White space should only appear in print work','A','Space carries meaning by grouping and by emphasis. Treating it as waste produces dense layouts that are slower to read.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Design principles','exam','A designer repeats a colour, a rule weight and a heading style across eight campaign assets. Which principle is being applied and to what end?','Contrast, to create tension','Repetition, to create a recognisable system so the set reads as one campaign','Proximity, to group items','Balance, to distribute weight','B','Repetition of a small set of decisions is what makes separate assets legible as one campaign. It is the mechanism behind visual consistency.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Typography','hard','A body text setting uses 9 point type with tight leading and full justification in narrow columns. What is the main legibility issue?','The typeface is too decorative','The colour is wrong','Justification in narrow measure creates uneven word spacing and rivers, and tight leading compounds it at small sizes','There are too few paragraphs','C','Narrow measure gives the justification algorithm too little room, producing gaps and rivers. Small type with tight leading makes those defects harder to read past.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Typography','exam','What is the difference between kerning and tracking?','They are the same operation','Tracking changes the typeface weight','Kerning applies only to headlines','Kerning adjusts the space between a specific pair of characters, while tracking adjusts spacing uniformly across a range of text','D','Kerning is a pair-level correction, typically applied to display type. Tracking is a uniform adjustment across a run of text.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Typography','exam','How many typefaces should a small campaign system typically use, and why?','One or two families, using weight, size and case for variation, so the system stays coherent and production stays manageable','As many as possible for variety','Exactly five','Only system default fonts','A','A restricted family set with a wide weight range gives variation without fragmenting the identity. It also reduces licensing and production overhead.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Typography','hard','An Arabic and an English headline are set at the same point size but the Arabic appears visually smaller and lighter. What is the correct treatment?','Leave it, point size equality is correct','Adjust the Arabic size and leading optically so the two match in perceived weight and presence, since scripts differ in x-height and stroke construction','Apply a bold weight to the Arabic in all cases','Convert both to outlines','B','Point size measures the em box, not perceived size, and Arabic letterforms occupy it differently. Optical matching is the professional standard for bilingual setting.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Typography','exam','A font licence covers desktop use only. The client wants the font embedded in a website. What is required?','Nothing, desktop licences cover web use','The font must be renamed','A separate webfont licence must be obtained for the domain and traffic level','Converting text to images removes the licence requirement','C','Desktop and web use are separately licensed rights. Serving a font file to browsers without a webfont licence breaches the agreement.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Typography','exam','What is the practical purpose of converting type to outlines before sending artwork to a printer?','It reduces the colour count','It converts CMYK to RGB','It improves the resolution','It removes the dependency on the font being present or licensed at the output stage, at the cost of the text no longer being editable','D','Outlining guarantees the letterforms render as designed regardless of the fonts installed. The trade-off is permanent loss of editability, so a live-text copy must be retained.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Colour','exam','Body text is set in mid grey on a light grey background and fails an accessibility check. What is the correct remedy?','Increase the contrast ratio between text and background to meet the minimum required for the text size','Increase the font size only','Add a drop shadow','Change the typeface','A','Accessibility for text is governed by the measured contrast ratio. Effects and typeface choices do not change the measured ratio.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Colour','hard','Why can a colour that looks correct on screen print differently?','The printer is faulty','Screens emit additive RGB light with a wider gamut than CMYK inks, so out-of-gamut colours shift when converted','Print always uses more ink','Screen colour is measured in pixels','B','The two systems have different gamuts and colours outside the print gamut must be mapped. Proofing and profiles are how that shift is controlled.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Colour','exam','What is the function of a colour profile in a managed workflow?','It compresses the file','It sets the resolution','It describes how colour values map to appearance on a specific device, allowing consistent conversion between devices','It locks the layers','C','A profile characterises a device colour space so conversions preserve appearance. Without profiles, values are interpreted differently at each stage.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Colour','hard','A brand palette relies on colour alone to distinguish three states in a chart. What is the accessibility failure and the fix?','No failure, colour is sufficient','Only the legend needs changing','The chart should be removed','Colour is not perceivable by all users, so state must also be encoded by a second channel such as label, shape or pattern','D','Encoding information in colour alone excludes users with colour vision deficiency and fails in monochrome output. A redundant non-colour channel resolves it.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Colour','exam','Which colour relationship describes two hues opposite each other on the colour wheel, used to create strong contrast?','Complementary','Analogous','Monochromatic','Triadic','A','Complementary hues sit opposite one another and produce maximum hue contrast. Analogous hues are adjacent and monochromatic uses one hue.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Image editing','exam','A logo must be scaled from a business card to a vehicle wrap without loss. What must be true of the file?','It must be a high resolution JPEG','It must be vector artwork, since vectors are resolution independent','It must be a PNG with transparency','It must be at 300 pixels per inch','B','Vector artwork is described mathematically and rescales without degradation. Any raster format has a fixed pixel count and degrades on enlargement.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Image editing','exam','Why should adjustments be applied as adjustment layers rather than directly to the image pixels?','It makes the file smaller','It converts the image to vector','It keeps the edit non-destructive, so the original pixels are preserved and the adjustment can be changed or removed later','It is required for print','C','Non-destructive editing preserves the source and keeps every decision reversible. Direct pixel edits are permanent once flattened and saved.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Image editing','hard','Which selection approach is most appropriate for isolating a product with a hard, well-defined edge from its background?','Freehand lasso at low zoom','Erasing the background with a soft brush','A single click of the magic wand at default tolerance','A pen or path based selection refined at high zoom, converted to a mask','D','A path gives a precise, editable edge and converts cleanly to a mask. Erasing is destructive and tolerance-based clicks rarely follow a hard edge accurately.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Image editing','hard','A composite places a product photographed under warm light onto a background photographed under cool daylight. It looks wrong even though the cut-out is perfect. What is the cause and fix?','Lighting direction and colour temperature do not match, so the product needs colour grading and shadow work consistent with the background light','The resolution differs; upscale the product','The file format is wrong','The background must be blurred','A','Believable composites require consistent light colour, direction and contact shadows. A clean edge cannot compensate for mismatched lighting.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Image editing','exam','What does a layer mask allow that deleting pixels does not?','A smaller file size','Reversible concealment of pixels, with the ability to refine or remove the concealment at any time','Automatic colour correction','Conversion to CMYK','B','A mask hides rather than destroys, so the edit can be refined indefinitely. Deletion discards the information permanently.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Publishing and export','exam','Which format should be used for a photographic image on a web page where file size matters and transparency is not needed?','TIFF','BMP','A compressed web format such as JPEG or WebP at a tuned quality setting','EPS','C','Photographic content compresses well in lossy web formats at a tuned quality. Print and uncompressed formats are far too large for delivery.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Publishing and export','exam','Which format is appropriate for a logo used on a web page that must stay crisp at any size and support transparency?','JPEG','Uncompressed TIFF','BMP','SVG','D','SVG is vector and scales without loss while supporting transparency. JPEG is raster and has no transparency channel.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Publishing and export','exam','What should be checked in a preflight before sending a document to print?','Resolution of linked images, colour mode and profiles, bleed and margins, font availability or outlining, and overprint or transparency issues','Only the page count','The name of the designer','The number of layers','A','Preflight verifies exactly the conditions that cause press failures. A checklist of resolution, colour, bleed, fonts and transparency covers the common causes.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Publishing and export','hard','A client reports that the exported PDF looks correct on screen but prints with visible banding in a gradient. What is the most likely cause?','The monitor is uncalibrated','The gradient is being reproduced with insufficient tonal steps for the output device, and it should be rebuilt with added noise or a higher bit depth and exported with appropriate transparency flattening','The PDF version is too new','The document has too many layers','B','Banding appears when the output device cannot resolve enough steps across the gradient. Adding fine noise and preserving bit depth through export is the standard remedy.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Publishing and export','exam','Why should assets be exported at multiple pixel densities for digital delivery?','To satisfy the file naming convention','Because file size is unimportant on the web','Because high density displays render low resolution assets softly, so a higher density version is needed alongside the standard one','Because vector formats cannot be used online','C','High density screens map several device pixels to each layout pixel and reveal insufficient resolution. Providing a higher density export keeps the asset crisp.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Publishing and export','exam','What is the purpose of a naming and versioning convention for delivered files?','It satisfies the printer software','It replaces the need for a preflight','It reduces the file size','It makes the correct, current file unambiguous to everyone downstream and prevents an outdated version being published','D','Ambiguous file names are a common cause of the wrong version being printed or published. A convention removes that ambiguity for everyone downstream.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Design principles','exam','A social advertisement must communicate one idea in under two seconds of scrolling. Which composition decision matters most?','A single dominant focal point with a short high-contrast headline, with detail moved to the accompanying text','Including every product benefit','A dense border treatment','Using at least four typefaces','A','At scrolling speed only one idea can be received, so the composition must have a single focal point. Detail belongs where it can be read at leisure.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Working in the design industry','exam','A stakeholder asks for a change late in production that would break the agreed specification. What is the professional handling?','Refuse without explanation','Set out the effect on schedule, cost and the agreed specification, offer an option that meets the intent within scope, and record the decision','Make the change silently','Escalate to the client executive immediately','B','Change is handled by making its consequences visible and offering a route that preserves the intent. Recording the decision protects both parties.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Colour','exam','What is a spot colour and when is it specified?','Any colour used more than once','A colour used only in digital output','A pre-mixed ink specified when an exact colour must be reproduced consistently or when it lies outside the CMYK gamut','A colour created by the printer automatically','C','Spot inks are mixed to a standard rather than built from process inks. They are specified for exact brand colours and out-of-gamut colours.'),
('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design','Typography','exam','Which line length is generally recommended for comfortable reading of body text?','Around 20 characters per line','Line length has no effect on reading comfort','Around 120 characters per line','Roughly 45 to 75 characters per line including spaces','D','Very short measures break the reading rhythm and very long ones make line tracking difficult. The mid-range is the long-standing typographic recommendation.')
) as v(certification, syllabus_area, difficulty, question, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_option, rationale)
where not exists (select 1 from public.certification_exam_question where certification = 'Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design');

-- ============================================================================
-- CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree (CXL) — 40 questions
-- ============================================================================
insert into public.certification_exam_question
  (certification, syllabus_area, difficulty, question, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_option, rationale)
select * from (values
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Conversion research','exam','A marketplace landing page converts at 1.1%. Where should an optimisation programme begin?','With conversion research, combining heuristic analysis, analytics, session recordings, on-site polls and user testing to locate where and why visitors fail','With a test of the button colour','With a full site redesign','With increasing traffic to the page','A','Research identifies the actual points of failure so that tests address real problems. Testing without research spends traffic on guesses.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Conversion research','exam','What does heuristic analysis contribute that analytics cannot?','Exact conversion rates by segment','A structured expert walkthrough that identifies likely friction, clarity and motivation problems, generating hypotheses that analytics can then size','Statistical significance','Traffic volume','B','Analytics reports what happened but not why it happened. A structured walkthrough generates the candidate explanations that data then prioritises.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Conversion research','exam','Which qualitative method best reveals why buyers hesitate at the quotation request form?','A brand tracking survey','A competitor teardown','On-page exit polls and moderated user tests on the form itself, asking what is unclear or concerning','A keyword volume report','C','Asking users at the point of hesitation captures the reason while it is live. Brand and market instruments operate at the wrong level of detail.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Conversion research','hard','Session recordings show many visitors scrolling past a value proposition block. The team proposes deleting it. What is the more rigorous reading?','Delete it, since it is being ignored','Keep it unchanged because it is on brand','Recordings are not valid evidence','Scroll-past behaviour indicates the block is not earning attention where it sits, which could be position, clarity or relevance, so the cause should be identified before removal is tested','D','Being skipped is a symptom with several possible causes. Removing a block that is merely mis-positioned discards value that a placement or clarity change would recover.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Conversion research','exam','What is the purpose of a customer survey asking what almost stopped a buyer from submitting a request?','To surface the specific objections and missing information that the page can then address, in the customers own language','To produce a satisfaction score','To measure brand awareness','To recruit new customers','A','Objections stated in the customers own words become the copy and the content of the page. That language is more persuasive than internally authored phrasing.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Conversion research','exam','A team has no budget for a research tool. Which zero-cost research is still available?','None; research requires paid tools','Analytics funnel and segment analysis, reading sales and support conversations, and structured heuristic review of the journey','Only competitor analysis','Only a redesign','B','Sales conversations, support tickets and existing analytics carry most of the objection and friction evidence already. A structured review of them costs nothing but time.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Hypothesis and prioritisation','exam','Which is a properly formed optimisation hypothesis?','Change the headline to something better','Redesign the page','Because research shows visitors do not understand who the marketplace serves, stating the buyer segment and the outcome in the headline will increase the request submission rate for paid traffic','Test the colour of the button','C','A hypothesis names the evidence, the change, the expected effect and the metric and audience it applies to. Without those it cannot be evaluated.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Hypothesis and prioritisation','exam','Why must a hypothesis state the primary metric before the test runs?','It is a reporting formality','It shortens the test','It increases the sample size','It prevents the outcome being chosen after the fact from whichever metric happened to move, which would invalidate the result','D','Choosing a metric after seeing the data is a form of selective reporting that manufactures false wins. Pre-committing removes that freedom.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Hypothesis and prioritisation','exam','A backlog holds 40 test ideas and the site supports two tests a month. What should govern the order?','A prioritisation model weighing expected impact, confidence in the evidence and the effort or traffic required','The seniority of whoever suggested each idea','Alphabetical order','The newest ideas first','A','Limited testing capacity must be spent where expected value per unit of effort is highest. Prioritisation models make that trade explicit and reviewable.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Hypothesis and prioritisation','hard','Two ideas have equal expected impact. Idea A rests on three independent research findings; idea B rests on one stakeholder opinion. Traffic is scarce. Which runs first and why?','Idea B, because it is faster to build','Idea A, because higher confidence in the underlying evidence raises the expected value of spending scarce traffic on it','Both simultaneously on the same page','Neither; gather more research','B','With equal impact, confidence in the evidence decides. Scarce traffic should be spent where the prior probability of a real effect is highest.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Hypothesis and prioritisation','exam','What is the risk of testing many small, low-impact changes on a low-traffic site?','There is no risk','Small changes always win','Small effects require very large samples to detect, so a low-traffic site will spend months without a readable result','It uses too much developer time only','C','Detectable effect size falls as sample grows, and low traffic caps the achievable sample. Low-traffic sites must test larger, bolder changes.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Testing statistics','exam','A test needs to detect a relative uplift of 10% on a baseline conversion rate of 2%, at 80% power and 95% confidence. What follows for planning?','The test can be read after 200 visitors','Sample size does not need calculating for two variations','Significance will appear within a day','A required sample per variation must be calculated in advance, and the test run to that sample or the planned duration, whichever is longer','D','Sample size is determined before the test by the baseline, the effect to detect, power and confidence. Reading before that sample is reached invites a false result.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Testing statistics','exam','What does peeking at a test daily and stopping when significance first appears do to the result?','It inflates the false positive rate substantially, because repeated looks each carry a chance of crossing the threshold by chance','Nothing, significance is significance','It increases statistical power','It shortens the required sample legitimately','A','Every additional look is another opportunity for random variation to cross the threshold. Stopping on the first crossing systematically manufactures winners.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Testing statistics','hard','What does a p-value of 0.04 mean in an A/B test?','There is a 96% chance the variation is better','If there were truly no difference, a result at least this extreme would occur about 4% of the time','The variation will produce 4% more revenue','The test has 96% power','B','The p-value is the probability of the observed data under the null hypothesis, not the probability that the hypothesis is true. It says nothing about effect size.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Testing statistics','hard','A test reaches significance at day 3 with a 42% uplift on 300 conversions total. The team wants to ship it. What is the professional advice?','Ship it, the uplift is large','Stop the test and declare no result','Continue to the pre-calculated sample and at least one full business cycle, since early large effects regress and a 3-day window can miss weekday and weekend behaviour','Restart the test with a new hypothesis','C','Early significant results are systematically overstated and regress toward the true effect. Running a full cycle also removes day-of-week composition effects.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Testing statistics','exam','Why should a test run for at least one full week, and preferably whole weeks?','Platform requirements','It reduces the cost of the test','It increases the conversion rate','Traffic composition and behaviour vary by day of week, so partial weeks bias the sample toward particular visitor types','D','Cutting a test mid-week overweights some days and their visitor mix. Whole weeks keep the composition of each variation comparable.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Testing statistics','hard','What is statistical power in the context of a conversion test?','The probability of detecting a real effect of a given size when one exists','The probability that a winning variation is implemented','The size of the observed uplift','The confidence level','A','Power is the chance of not missing a real effect of the stated size. Confidence governs false positives, power governs false negatives.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Testing statistics','hard','A test is declared a winner overall, but a segment analysis run afterwards shows the effect is confined to mobile and reversed on desktop. What is the correct handling?','Ship the change everywhere on the overall result','Treat the segment finding as a hypothesis rather than a result, since it was not pre-specified, and validate it with a properly powered test on that segment','Ship it to mobile only, the segment result is conclusive','Discard the whole test','B','Post hoc segment splits are underpowered and multiply the chance of a spurious pattern. They generate hypotheses that must then be tested on their own terms.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Testing statistics','exam','An A/B/C/D test compares four variations on a single primary metric. What must be accounted for?','Nothing, more variations is always better','The confidence level must be lowered','Multiple comparisons increase the chance that at least one variation appears to win by chance, and the required sample rises with each arm','Power is unaffected by arm count','C','Each additional arm adds another opportunity for a chance crossing and divides the traffic. Both effects must be planned for before launch.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Testing statistics','exam','A site receives 3,000 sessions and 60 requests a month. What is the realistic testing programme?','Weekly A/B tests on small elements','No optimisation is possible','Multivariate testing with eight combinations','Few, large tests aimed at substantial effects, run over long periods, supplemented by qualitative research and reasoned best practice','D','At that volume only large effects are detectable in a reasonable time. Research and judgement carry the programme between the rare tests that can be read.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Testing statistics','hard','What is a sample ratio mismatch and why does it matter?','A significant deviation from the intended traffic split between variations, which signals an instrumentation or delivery fault invalidating the test','A difference in conversion rates between variations','A difference in device mix','A change in the baseline rate','A','An unintended split means the randomisation or delivery is broken. Any comparison built on a broken assignment is untrustworthy regardless of its p-value.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Experimentation programme','exam','What should be recorded for every completed test, win or loss?','Only the winners','The hypothesis, the evidence behind it, the design, the sample, the primary metric, the result with its uncertainty and the decision taken','The name of the designer only','A screenshot of the winning variation','B','A complete record is what turns individual tests into cumulative organisational learning. Losses often carry more information than wins.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Experimentation programme','exam','Why are losing tests valuable?','They are not; only wins matter','They increase the win rate','They falsify a belief the team held, which prevents that belief being built into future work and redirects effort','They improve statistical power','C','A disproved assumption is durable knowledge that stops the same mistake recurring. Programmes that only record wins keep repeating the failures.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Experimentation programme','exam','A stakeholder demands a change with no supporting evidence and refuses testing. What is the professional response?','Refuse the change outright','Escalate immediately without proposing an option','Implement it silently and report a win','Implement it as a test where possible so the decision is measured rather than argued, and state the risk if it must ship untested','D','Converting an opinion into a measurable test removes the argument without blocking the stakeholder. Where testing is impossible, the risk should at least be recorded.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Experimentation programme','hard','A team reports a 65% test win rate. What should this prompt?','Scepticism, since unusually high win rates typically indicate peeking, underpowered tests, post hoc metric selection or validation errors','Celebration and expansion of the programme','An immediate increase in traffic allocation','Nothing; win rate is not a meaningful figure','A','Mature programmes report win rates far below this. An exceptional rate is more often evidence of methodological error than of exceptional ideas.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Experimentation programme','exam','What is the correct treatment of an inconclusive test?','Ship the variation that was numerically ahead','Record it as inconclusive, keep the current experience, and decide whether the hypothesis merits a better powered retest','Declare it a loss and abandon the hypothesis','Rerun it until it becomes significant','B','Inconclusive means the data could not distinguish the options, so the incumbent stays. Rerunning until significance appears is the peeking error in another form.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Landing page optimisation','exam','Which element most commonly limits conversion on a paid traffic landing page for a B2B marketplace?','The footer navigation','The favicon','Clarity of who the offer is for and what happens next, together with the friction of the request form','The number of images','C','Clarity and friction are the two dominant levers, repeatedly demonstrated across lead generation pages. Peripheral elements rarely move the primary metric.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Landing page optimisation','exam','What is message match and why does it affect the conversion rate?','Matching the brand colours across pages','Matching the font to the logo','Matching the page to competitor pages','Continuity between the query or advertisement promise and the page headline and offer, which sustains the visitors expectation and reduces immediate abandonment','D','A visitor arrives holding a specific expectation, and a page that restates it confirms they are in the right place. A mismatch produces immediate exits.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Landing page optimisation','exam','A form asks for eleven fields to request a quotation. What is the standard optimisation and its trade-off?','Reduce to the fields needed to route and respond, which usually raises submissions, with the trade-off that some qualification moves to a later step','Add more fields to qualify harder','Remove the form entirely','Split it into eleven separate pages','A','Each required field costs completions, so only the routing-critical fields belong at first submission. The qualification work then moves downstream rather than disappearing.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Landing page optimisation','hard','Reducing a form from eleven fields to four raises submissions by 60% but the sales team reports a fall in qualified leads. How should this be judged?','A clear win, submissions rose','On cost per qualified lead and on downstream close rate, since the primary metric should be the qualified outcome rather than the raw submission','A clear loss, revert immediately','The two results are unrelated','B','A form change moves both volume and quality, so it must be judged on the outcome the business sells. Only cost per qualified lead settles it.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Landing page optimisation','exam','Which form of social proof is most persuasive to a procurement manager evaluating a marketplace?','A generic five-star badge','A stock photograph of a team','Named references from comparable organisations with specific outcomes, and verifiable counts of suppliers and completed transactions','The number of social media followers','C','Relevance and specificity make proof credible to a professional buyer. Generic badges and vanity counts carry little evidential weight.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Landing page optimisation','exam','How should an Arabic version of a landing page be optimised?','Translate the winning English page and ship it','Only translate the headline','Assume the English test results transfer','Treat it as a separate optimisation surface with its own research, native copy, mirrored layout and its own test results, since the audience and language differ','D','Test results are specific to the audience and the execution that produced them. Arabic requires its own research, native copy, mirrored layout and its own evidence.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Landing page optimisation','exam','What is the role of the call to action label on a lead generation page?','To state the specific next action and what the visitor receives, reducing uncertainty at the point of commitment','Purely decorative','To match the brand typeface','To fill the remaining space','A','A specific label tells the visitor exactly what happens next and lowers perceived risk. Vague labels leave the commitment ambiguous.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Analytics for optimisation','exam','Before any testing begins, what must be verified about the analytics implementation?','That the dashboard looks attractive','That the conversion event fires exactly once per genuine outcome, on all templates and devices, and that the figure reconciles with the system of record','That all reports are shared with the team','That data retention is set to 14 months','B','A test can only be as trustworthy as the measurement beneath it. Verifying the event and reconciling it with the system of record must precede any experiment.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Analytics for optimisation','exam','Why is segmenting the conversion rate more useful than reporting a single site-wide figure?','It produces larger numbers','Segments always have higher rates','A single figure averages away large differences between traffic sources, devices and intents, hiding both the problems and the opportunities','It reduces the sample size needed','C','Aggregate rates conceal opposing movements in the segments beneath them. Segmentation is what locates the actual problem.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Analytics for optimisation','hard','Overall conversion rate is flat month on month, yet mobile fell from 2.4% to 1.6% and desktop rose from 3.0% to 3.6%. What is the correct conclusion?','Nothing changed, the site is stable','The measurement is broken','Desktop improvements should be rolled out to mobile','Two opposing movements are cancelling in the aggregate, so a mobile regression must be investigated regardless of the flat headline','D','A flat aggregate can conceal offsetting changes in its components. The mobile decline is a real regression and must be diagnosed on its own.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Analytics for optimisation','exam','What is a micro conversion and how should it be used?','A smaller intermediate action that indicates progress toward the main outcome, used as a diagnostic and occasionally as a proxy metric on low-traffic tests','A conversion worth less than one dirham','A conversion on mobile only','A conversion that failed','A','Micro conversions locate where progression breaks and, being more frequent, can support a reading where the primary outcome is too rare. They remain a proxy and not the goal.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Analytics for optimisation','exam','A test tool and the analytics platform report different conversion counts for the same variation. What must happen before the result is used?','Use the larger of the two numbers','Reconcile the discrepancy by checking the event definitions, deduplication and assignment, since an unexplained gap undermines the whole result','Average the two figures','Ignore analytics and trust the test tool','B','An unexplained measurement gap means at least one system is wrong about the outcome. The result cannot be relied on until the cause is identified.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Conversion research','exam','A team wants to understand why suppliers abandon registration. Which combination gives the most complete picture?','Analytics alone','Interviews alone','Funnel analytics to locate the step, session recordings to see the behaviour, and interviews or exit polls with abandoners to learn the reason','A competitor teardown alone','C','Analytics locates the step, recordings show the behaviour and direct contact supplies the reason. Each method answers a different part of the question.'),
('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree','Experimentation programme','exam','What is the correct relationship between conversion optimisation and paid media on a small budget?','They are independent functions','Media should be paused during optimisation','Optimisation only matters at high budgets','Raising landing page conversion lowers the cost per acquisition for every dirham of media already being spent, so optimisation multiplies the existing budget','D','Conversion rate divides into the cost of every acquisition, so improving it improves all media simultaneously. That leverage matters most when the budget is small.')
) as v(certification, syllabus_area, difficulty, question, option_a, option_b, option_c, option_d, correct_option, rationale)
where not exists (select 1 from public.certification_exam_question where certification = 'CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree');

-- ============================================================================
-- Proof: every certification in this batch must hold at least 40 questions.
-- ============================================================================
do $$
declare
  v_missing text;
begin
  select string_agg(format('%s=%s', c.name, coalesce(q.n, 0)), ', ' order by c.name)
    into v_missing
  from (values
    ('CIM Level 6 Diploma in Professional Marketing'),
    ('Google Analytics 4 Certification'),
    ('CDMP-DMI (Certified Digital Marketing Professional)'),
    ('Meta Certified Digital Marketing Associate'),
    ('Adobe Certified Professional in Visual Design'),
    ('CXL Conversion Optimization Minidegree')
  ) as c(name)
  left join (
    select certification, count(*) as n
    from public.certification_exam_question
    group by certification
  ) q on q.certification = c.name
  where coalesce(q.n, 0) < 40;

  if v_missing is not null then
    raise exception 'certifications_growth: bank(s) below 40 questions: %', v_missing;
  end if;
end $$;
